<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dutch–Indonesian Round Table Conference</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1949</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesian-national-revolution">Indonesian National Revolution</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a>–Indonesian Round Table Conference met in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-hague">The Hague</a> from August to November 1949, bringing together the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a> and the federal states created by the Dutch. It agreed that the Netherlands would transfer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> to the Republic of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> of Indonesia, which took place on 27 December 1949, while the status of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-guinea">New Guinea</a> was left for later talks. Indonesia also took over much of the colonial debt.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dutch-indonesian-round-table-conference.jpg" alt="Dutch–Indonesian Round Table Conference" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Daan Noske / Anefo · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ronde_Tafel_Conferentie_,_slotzitting_in_Ridderzaal,_Hatta_tekent,_Bestanddeelnr_903-6874.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
